      "content": "thanks for the quick turnaround. i was talking to the systems team about those latency issues you mentioned, and they suggested that the predictive maintenance module might be too \"heavy\" on the compute side. \n\nthey want to push a firmware patch to the fleet tonight to streamline the logic and reduce the processing overhead. it'll basically simplify the decision-making parameters so the ships aren't constantly recalculating complex routes, which should stop the spikes. can you check the patch manifest and see if there are any conflicts with the current routing protocols before i authorize the deployment?",
